I vote for the explicit maximize_likelihood which makes it clear what
the optimization criterion is (recall that much of ML is dedicated to
criteria outside of maximizing likelihood).  Actually, it should be
maximize_posterior_density.  maximize_likelihood should just trigger
a “No-Frequentists Club” warning.

